; DIMLINEAR options (PT26, #713): Text with <> (the value takes its place),
; Angle (explicit text angle), Horizontal and Vertical against the automatic
; choice, Rotated 30 degrees. Prompts from autocad-quote.txt (dxf-test-file
; 1ad04b0): after Text and Rotated the full prompt comes back; after
; Horizontal and Vertical only [Text/Angle] (Mtext left out, decision of
; 2026-11-11). With a replaced text AutoCAD still ends with the measured
; value ("Dimension text = 50" after "<> mm").
; Values by hand from PT23 with ISO-25, as in
; dimlinear/punti-direzione-automatica: six graphics records, numbered after
; the dimension, for a text above the line. With an explicit text angle
; (Angle) the text is centred in the middle of the dimension line, which
; breaks around it (PT23, point 4; decision of the maintainer on #712):
; text-point 10,35 and seven graphics records (two extension lines, two
; pieces of dimension line, two arrows, the text), so the next dimensions
; are 272, 279 and 286. Rotated: origins 0,120 and 0,160,
; u = (cos 30, sin 30), measurement 40 sin 30 = 20.
DIMLINEAR
0,0
50,0
T
<> mm
25,10
DIMLINEAR
0,20
0,50
A
90
10,35
DIMLINEAR
0,60
30,100
H
40,80
DIMLINEAR
60,60
100,90
V
80,120
DIMLINEAR
0,120
0,160
R
30
-20,150
